description:
Develop a delay block that introduces a configurable delay to a single-bit input signal. The module utilizes a shift register to store the incoming signal, implementing the specified delay time in nanoseconds. On each clock cycle, the least significant bit of the shift register is shifted out and replaced by the incoming signal. The output reflects the value of the input signal after it has been delayed by the predetermined number of clock cycles, effectively serving as a time delay element in digital circuits.
module top_module(
  input wire in,
  input wire clk,
  output wire out
);

code:
module top_module(
  input wire in,
  input wire clk,
  output wire out
);parameter delay_time = 10; // in bits for shifting

// define shift register
reg [delay_time-1:0] shift_register;

// shift register input and output
always @(posedge clk) begin
  shift_register <= {shift_register[delay_time-2:0], in};
end

assign out = shift_register[delay_time-1];

endmodule

