description:
Design a circuit that implements a left shift operation on a 16-bit input. The module continuously shifts the input left by 4 bits while operating under a clock signal, and it is capable of handling an input reset. The shifting operation only occurs after the input has been received for ten clock cycles; prior to that, the module counts clock cycles and maintains the input value. Once the shifting begins, the output reflects the shifted value, and a valid signal is asserted to indicate that the output is ready.
module top_module(/*AUTOARG*/
   // Outputs
   out,
   valid,
   // Inputs
   clk, reset, in
   );

