Design a binary to BCD (Binary-Coded Decimal) converter that takes a 4-bit binary input and produces an 8-bit BCD output. The module processes the binary input through a series of stages, first forwarding the input value, and then applying correction factors based on comparisons with the values 5 and 10 to adjust the binary number into its BCD representation. The final output concatenates the converted digits, allowing it to represent decimal values in a form suitable for display or further processing.
